\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Corner-to-corner first passage on the square lattice, $N=35$, $q=0.8$, discrete time. (a)~Exact PMF from time stepping (line) and histogram of $4\times 10^{6}$ simulated walkers in bins of 200 steps (circles; bars are $\pm 2$ standard errors and are smaller than the symbols). Dashed line: mode $t^{*}=2493$; dotted line: mean $T=14\,100.8$. (b)~Relative error of three numerical inversions of the generating function against the exact PMF: the trapezoidal rule on a circle of fixed radius $r=0.9$ truncated after $K=54$ nodes, the same rule with all $2t$ nodes, and the rule \eqref  {s3_methods:eq-aw} with $\gamma =10$. The two fixed-radius curves leave the frame near $t=700$; at $t^{*}$ (dashed) the truncated fixed-radius rule returns $3.6\times 10^{93}$.}}{7}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
